<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Great Peacemaker</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Deganawida, Dekanawida, the Peacemaker</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Great Peacemaker, Deganawida, is the founder of the Iroquois Confederacy in Haudenosaunee tradition. Said to have been born among the Huron, he brought a message of peace to the warring Mohawk, Oneida, Onondaga, Cayuga and Seneca and, with his spokesman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hiawatha">Hiawatha</a>, persuaded them to accept the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-law-of-peace">Great Law of Peace</a>. His dating is uncertain, with estimates ranging from the 12th to the 16th century.</p></div>
